From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 15:35:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: sm8150: map the ports of every SLIMbus link

sm8150_dai_init() runs once per DAI link, but for_each_rtd_codec_dais()
only walks the codec DAIs belonging to the link currently being
initialised. The slim_port_setup flag, however, is stored per card, so
the very first SLIMbus back end to be initialised consumes it and every
later SLIMbus link returns before its codec DAI is ever given a channel
map.

That is harmless on a board with a single SLIMbus back end, which is why
it has not been noticed. On hotdog there are two: SLIMBUS_6_RX to
AIF4_PB for headphone playback, and SLIMBUS_0_TX to AIF1_CAP for
microphone capture. Whichever is initialised first wins, so AIF1_CAP
keeps an empty slim_ch_list, wcd934x_get_channel_map() reports zero TX
channels, no SLIMbus TX port is ever opened, and capture returns a
perfectly running stream of digital silence.

Map the ports of every SLIMbus link instead. The flag now guards only
the jack registration, which really is a per-component operation and
must not be repeated.

Signed-off-by: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/sm8150.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8150.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8150.c
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8150.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8150.c
@@ -264,8 +264,7 @@

 	switch (cpu_dai->id) {
 	case SLIMBUS_0_RX...SLIMBUS_6_TX:
-		/* setting up wcd multiple times for slim port is redundant */
-		if (pdata->slim_port_setup || !link->no_pcm)
+		if (!link->no_pcm)
 			return 0;

 		for_each_rtd_codec_dais(rtd, i, codec_dai) {
@@ -281,6 +280,10 @@
 					       WCD934X_DEFAULT_MCLK_RATE,
 					       SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK);

+			/* the jack belongs to the component, not the link */
+			if (pdata->slim_port_setup)
+				continue;
+
 			rval = snd_soc_component_set_jack(codec_dai->component,
 							  &pdata->jack, NULL);
 			if (rval != 0 && rval != -ENOTSUPP) {
--
2.50.1
